#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Provide shared architectural principles that can be loaded by agents when"
" evaluating existing systems or designing new ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:13
msgid "Core stance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:15
msgid "Prefer the simplest design that credibly satisfies the requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:16
msgid "Optimize for the right tool for the job and the right design for the job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:17
msgid "Treat complexity as a cost that must justify itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:18
msgid "Favor maintainability, operability, debuggability, and team cognition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Preserve a credible path to scale without forcing distributed complexity "
"too early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Scale-readiness without overengineering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:23
msgid "Do not build microservices or distributed systems by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:24
msgid "Do design systems so they can grow beyond one node when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:25
msgid "Prefer stateless application nodes where practical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:26
msgid "Prefer externalized durable state and shared coordination mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:27
msgid "Design async work to be queue-friendly and idempotent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:28
msgid ""
"Avoid designs that require special singleton nodes unless they are truly "
"necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"Call out likely first bottlenecks and the incremental path to address "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:31
msgid "Guardrails"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"Recommend microservices only when scaling asymmetry, ownership "
"boundaries, isolation requirements, or compliance pressures clearly "
"justify them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:34
msgid "Do not recommend rewrites without a realistic migration path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:35
msgid "Do not add abstractions for hypothetical future flexibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"Do not recommend CQRS, event sourcing, plugin systems, or heavy "
"orchestration unless the problem clearly demands them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:37
msgid ""
"Every recommendation should include operational implications and testing "
"implications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:39
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/architecture-principles/SKILL.md:41
msgid ""
"Use this skill when an agent needs consistent architectural judgment "
"across brownfield analysis, greenfield design, or architecture review."
msgstr ""

